{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01IZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Z \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$Z$", "MATH_0004": "$Z'$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$Z$", "MATH_0007": "$(Z, \\mathcal{O}_Z)$", "MATH_0008": "$Z$", "MATH_0009": "$Z$", "MATH_0010": "$X_{red}$", "MATH_0011": "$X$", "MATH_0012": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-reduced-closed-subscheme}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-reduced-induced-scheme}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5170ed898a56de424eb82520ec6ad1e6ec0b27cd234ca93e60764a073542434a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:80969fc4c069ece40d7d8948f3533d834b7dcc58049a3e4884802f91113d3105", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a closed subset.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>scheme structure on <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is given by a closed subscheme <MATH_0004> of\n<MATH_0005> whose underlying set is equal to <MATH_0006>. We often say\n``let <MATH_0007> be a scheme structure on <MATH_0008>'' to\nindicate this. The <TEXTITOPEN_0002>reduced induced scheme structure<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\non <MATH_0009> is the one constructed in Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0003>reduction <MATH_0010> of <MATH_0011><TEXTITCLOSE_0003> is the reduced induced scheme\nstructure on <MATH_0012> itself.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6d904f35dd46f2315ca92ae64a1ed088fda77987f7781841bfb1dade1c577395", "unit_id": "tag:01J4:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01IZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Z \\subset X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Z$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:556cb06fa1d4dded511ac6d95ea64f9f0b8081d871fc1cab88a33a30e1a079ca", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:17584943fd4df35a9186be9ae19134f0eeef53068a1d7e1450b9b23a4486b9f2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nOften when we say ``let <MATH_0001> be an irreducible component of <MATH_0002>''\nwe think of <MATH_0003> as a reduced closed subscheme of <MATH_0004> using the reduced induced\nscheme structure.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b65123280f07b60f6e0878948a09f8b76bfcf7ba70d5103ef0ccbb0d46914c8e", "unit_id": "tag:01IZ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "01IZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\setminus \\partial T$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\partial T = \\overline{T} \\setminus T$", "MATH_0008": "$T$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-reduced-induced-scheme}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-reduced-induced-locally-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:38dbead05d760e8b3ceb4abc519259ade9b15b46a7187caf431679186b331b16", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8477f528c733d81fcb6d9a5ad6758df356d5b58cf064039c5064c0dc31af937a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a locally closed subset.\nIn this situation we sometimes also use the phrase\n``reduced induced scheme structure on <MATH_0003>''. It refers\nto the reduced induced scheme structure from\nDefinition <REF_0001>\nwhen we view <MATH_0004> as a closed subset of the open subscheme \n<MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006>. Here\n<MATH_0007> is the ``boundary'' of <MATH_0008>\nin the topological space of <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:64f9c9868cdf4dc17bc909f81d1d305af914fccf343d9e1df58a760ef77ea03d", "unit_id": "tag:0F2L:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01IZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Z \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$f : Y \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$Z$", "MATH_0006": "$f(Y) \\subset Z$", "MATH_0007": "$Y \\to X$", "MATH_0008": "$Y \\to X_{red} \\to X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-map-into-reduction}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:39a08033d898cf84fc4b61cf5f079f756125c46488e9fefde886c3436c554492", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53403f0baca5d4b75e841d1b734b2eebd008166ef9b5d052ada74d759aa884ff", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a closed subscheme.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a reduced scheme.\nA morphism <MATH_0004> factors through <MATH_0005> if and only if\n<MATH_0006> (set theoretically). In particular, any\nmorphism <MATH_0007> factors as <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6376952fdafb1c110eba6d8b2329ff1479b2ff3c6aed3e686997c4f2167793c7", "unit_id": "tag:0356:statement"}
